From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 22:17:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] toolchain: gcc: no flexible array size without its
 object's initializer

Under LTO, a partition that does not define an object cannot see its
initializer, and GCC then took the size of an initialized flexible
array member of that object as zero: -fsanitize=object-size turned
every function there that reads the member into a trap. nftables'
ct_print() became a single trap in a UBSan build, and nft trapped
printing any rule with a ct expression.

Add a patch to GCC that takes such a member's size as unknown when the
initializer is not available, as it already does for an extern object.
It is meant for GCC upstream.

Signed-off-by: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 ...ize-without-its-object-s-initializer.patch | 44 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 44 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 toolchain/gcc/patches-15.x/991-tree-no-flexible-array-size-without-its-object-s-initializer.patch

diff --git a/toolchain/gcc/patches-15.x/991-tree-no-flexible-array-size-without-its-object-s-initializer.patch b/toolchain/gcc/patches-15.x/991-tree-no-flexible-array-size-without-its-object-s-initializer.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..3133e7f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/toolchain/gcc/patches-15.x/991-tree-no-flexible-array-size-without-its-object-s-initializer.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,44 @@
+From: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
+Subject: [PATCH] tree: no flexible array size without its object's initializer
+
+component_ref_size() takes the size of an initialized flexible array
+member from its object's initializer, and gives up (NULL_TREE) for an
+extern object, whose initializer it cannot see. An LTO partition other
+than the one that defines the object cannot see the initializer either:
+DECL_INITIAL is error_mark_node there. component_ref_size() then took the
+size of the struct alone, so the member looked empty, and
+-fsanitize=object-size turned every function that reads it in that
+partition into a trap. nftables' ct_print(), which walks a statically
+initialized flexible array of symbols, became a single trap under
+-flto -fsanitize=undefined -fsanitize-trap=undefined.
+
+Give up as for an extern object when the initializer is not available.
+
+gcc/ChangeLog:
+
+	* tree.cc (component_ref_size): Return NULL_TREE for a flexible
+	array member of an object whose initializer is error_mark_node.
+
+Signed-off-by: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
+---
+--- a/gcc/tree.cc
++++ b/gcc/tree.cc
+@@ -13502,13 +13502,16 @@
+       if (typematch)
+ 	{
+ 	  if (DECL_P (base)
+-	      && DECL_EXTERNAL (base)
++	      && (DECL_EXTERNAL (base)
++		  || DECL_INITIAL (base) == error_mark_node)
+ 	      && bt == basetype
+ 	      && *sam != special_array_member::int_0)
+ 	    /* The size of a flexible array member of an extern struct
+ 	       with no initializer cannot be determined (it's defined
+ 	       in another translation unit and can have an initializer
+-	       with an arbitrary number of elements).  */
++	       with an arbitrary number of elements).  Nor can it when the
++	       object's initializer is not available here, as in an LTO
++	       partition other than the one that defines the object.  */
+ 	    return NULL_TREE;
+ 
+ 	  /* Use the size of the base struct or, for interior zero-length
